    "field": "Paleoclimatology",
    "problem": "Previous direct atmospheric CO2 records from Antarctic ice cores were limited to the past 650,000 years, preventing an understanding of carbon cycle dynamics and the full range of natural CO2 variability during earlier, distinct glacial cycles.",
    "method": "Atmospheric carbon dioxide concentrations from 650,000 to 800,000 years ago are determined by analyzing air trapped in the EPICA Dome C ice core using dry extraction techniques coupled with laser absorption spectroscopy and gas chromatography.",
    "task": "The task is to extend the atmospheric carbon dioxide concentration record from 650,000 to 800,000 years before present by analyzing air trapped in the deepest section of the EPICA Dome C ice core from Antarctica.",
